## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about cost-aware request routing, a practical constraint in real llm-ops gateways.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant budgeting and isolation
- Per-model pricing and token estimation
- Atomic budget updates
- Fallback routing and quotas

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code for budget check and routing
async function routePrompt(tenant, tokens, model){
  const pricePerK = PRICE[tenant][model];
  const cost = Math.ceil(tokens/1000) * pricePerK;
  const ok = await Redis.decrbyfloat(`budget:${tenant}`, cost);
  if(ok >= 0){
    return forwardToModel(tenant, model);
  } else {
    // revert and fallback
    await Redis.incrbyfloat(`budget:${tenant}`, cost);
    return forwardToBackup(tenant);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for race conditions in budget updates across multiple workers?
- How would you handle dynamic price changes mid-session?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement cost-aware, latency-conscious routing in a simple, auditable way. Focuses on per-tenant accounting, model pricing, and practical test coverage.

## Key Concepts

- Cost-aware routing and SLA mapping
- Per-tenant ledger and budget enforcement
- Simple fallback behaviors and test plans

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: ledger update and routing decision
function routePrompt(tenant, prompt) {
  const remaining = tenant.budget - tenant.spent;
  for (const m of ['fast','balanced','accurate']) {
    if (cost(m, prompt) <= remaining && latency(m, prompt) <= tenant.sla[m]) {
      tenant.spent += cost(m, prompt);
      return m;
    }
  }
  return 'cached';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this to handle budget rollovers and monthly resets?
- How would you test this with A/B experiments across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical governance, privacy compliance, and performance in multi-tenant LLM ops, including policy versioning, KMS integration, and audit-ability under latency pressure.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant redaction policies (regex/ML)
